# tests/modifiers/letters.rxt — module `modifiers` (MOD-0.5c): the cheap
# per-letter semantics measured at [MOD-0.5a] ruling 1 — `s` (dot's set
# grows from 255 to 256 members), `U` (greed swap at quantifier
# construction, BOTH directions), and `n` (capturing-`(` hook consults
# state; plain `(...)` stops capturing, and a backreference to a
# never-captured group is a compile error). `m` and `J` are NOT here: per
# ruling 2 they are per-letter REFUSALS (`m` -> module 'assertions', `J` ->
# module 'named-groups') — see tests/modifiers/malformed_and_gate.rxt.
#
# ORACLE SPLIT: `(?s)` at pattern position 0 is valid python syntax
# (DOTALL is one of python's supported inline letters) and python-verified.
# `U` and `n` are not python flag letters AT ALL — `re.compile("(?U)...")`
# and `re.compile("(?n)...")` raise "unknown extension" regardless of
# position, in agreement with pcrec's REFUSAL reason if run gate-off, but
# here (with `features modifiers` enabled and the construct meant to
# COMPILE and MATCH) python simply cannot express these two letters, so
# every U/n match/nomatch block is `# pcre2-only`, measured against live
# libpcre2 10.46 (tests/probes/probe_mod05.c's "candidate cheap semantics"
# block, cross-checked with a throwaway scratchpad extension for the
# specific subjects used here).
#
# THE D33 §9.3 RECORD: run against the MOD-0.5a-gate binary via
#   PCREC=<binary> bash tests/harness/run.sh tests/modifiers/letters.rxt
# 6 cases total, 4 fail with "requires module 'modifiers'" (measured
# 2026-08-12). The other 2 already PASS today for reasons unrelated to the
# module: `pattern a.b` needs no `features` line at all (base grammar, not
# gated), and `(?n)(a)\1`'s `perr` is satisfied by today's blanket gate
# refusal just as well as by the eventual real diagnostic.

# ---- (?s): dot matches newline; plain dot does not -----------------------

pattern (?s)a.b
features modifiers
m "a\nb" 0 3

pattern a.b
n "a\nb"

# ---- (?U): greed swap, BOTH directions ------------------------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?U)a+
features modifiers
m "aaa" 0 1

# pcre2-only
pattern (?U)a+?
features modifiers
m "aaa" 0 3

# ---- (?n): plain (...) stops capturing; \1 to it is a compile error ------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?n)(a)
features modifiers
m "a" 0 1

pattern (?n)(a)\1
features modifiers
perr

# ---- R17 additions (checks critic, 2026-08-12): the port's own corners ----
# Three cell families that were "correct today, unguarded" — verified only
# in tests/probes/probe_mod05*.c, which is not part of `make test`. Each
# expectation below was re-verified against libpcre2 10.46 at the R17
# disposition (the probe headers carry the measured cells).

# (?aP): the ASCII-restrict sub-letter is a MEASURED NO-OP at options=0,
# and the port's `a`+sub lookahead is a second implementation of the
# grammar's rule (recognition vs semantics) — this is its only gate-on pin.
# pcre2-only
pattern (?aP)x
features modifiers
m "x" 0 1

# unset WINS regardless of side order within one run: (?i-i) and (?-ii)
# are BOTH case-sensitive (probe_mod05c.c). Guarded by the port's fixed
# set-then-unset apply order — these cells are what notice a reorder.
# pcre2-only
pattern (?i-i)a
features modifiers
n "A"
m "a" 0 1

# pcre2-only
pattern (?-ii)a
features modifiers
n "A"
m "a" 0 1
